model {
  extend basalt.modelGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "Request reliability reads only its windows' rows. Home rows inside the raw window are read through the pool time index, terminal finishes through the finish time index, and final attempts outside the raw window through their request identity; no predicate ORs those sets, because that shape scans the pool's whole history. Terminal evidence joins a Home row by its start key, and only a canonical UUID request identity can match. Counts, attribution and boundaries are unchanged."
      constraint "The availability check-in still runs every minute. Its request reliability figure is computed with each five-minute history capture, its windows ending at that capture, and the check-in reuses it while it is under six minutes old. A missing, failed or older figure is computed by the check-in and kept for the next ones, so a stopped capture still reaches capture_stale. Breach, failing-now and collection-unavailable signals keep their rules; real-time terminal and gateway evidence reaches them at the next capture instead of the next minute."
    }
  }
}
